WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.505 --> 00:00:06.006
Oh, my gosh, do you look beautiful.

00:00:08.592 --> 00:00:10.844
When I first started thinking
about this story,

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:13.013
Felix was a central character in my head,

00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:15.349
and I've always been reluctant
to work with Bill

00:00:15.557 --> 00:00:17.726
after 'Lost In Translation',
because I feel

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:19.144
people loved him so much in that

00:00:19.228 --> 00:00:20.395
and it's too much expectation.

00:00:20.479 --> 00:00:22.439
I could never do that again.

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:23.148
But I think if you could just

00:00:23.232 --> 00:00:25.567
have more energy
and quicker within the lines.

00:00:25.651 --> 00:00:26.944
But now after all these years,
I feel like...

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:28.570
I love working with him.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.405
We'll just go for it 
and try something,

00:00:30.531 --> 00:00:31.573
and it will be something different.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.658
Stand up.

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:33.951
-Put your arms around me.
-What?

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:37.287
Yuck.

00:00:39.248 --> 00:00:40.082
Action!

00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:41.333
I have a great trust in her.

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:44.169
I've been really fortunate to work
with people that are really good

00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:47.881
and fun, so when they call, 
I just go like, "Okay, it's Sofia."

00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:50.342
I feel like now that I've known Bill
all these years,

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:53.095
he's a friend and like a big brother who...

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:54.847
not unlike the character,
kind of just sweeps in and...

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.850
brings magic and life to the situation, 

00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:00.269
and so, he's sort of this fairy godfather.

00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:02.062
Does my foot smell funny?

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:02.980
Ew!

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.649
I'm having more fun
watching her all the time

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:06.900
I mean, she was just a child

00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:09.403
when she made this movie,
and she just keeps getting better.

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:11.780
Please wait a little longer before you exit.

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:13.156
Oh, sure.

00:01:13.407 --> 00:01:15.325
This movie is personal to me in that

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:17.661
it reflects where I've been living,

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.998
and details of parenthood
and struggling with being creative

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:22.291
and trying to find your footing.

00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:25.252
And in 'Lost In Translation',
it was a young woman in her 20s 

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:27.546
kind of finding herself
and now this is another phase,

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:29.089
and hopefully by the end,

00:01:29.173 --> 00:01:31.008
the characters have gotten 
something from each other.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:33.010
We all just want to be loved.

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:35.012
You've got beauty and character,

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.306
which is the most important thing
a person can have.

